            "FilePath": "",
            "Summary": "Defense-retained crime scene analyst (former FBI, 30 years) examined the rear exterior door and surrounding alley. Findings: (1) The rear door\u0027s lock was \u0027basic builder-grade\u0027 and could be opened with a credit card or simple bump key. (2) The doorframe showed signs of prior forced entry (scratches around the strike plate) — suggesting this was not the first time someone entered through this door. (3) The alley is a known drug transaction location with multiple prior police calls. (4) Three cigarette butts of different brands were found in the alley within 10 feet of the rear door — none matched Webb\u0027s brand. (5) A partial muddy footprint was found just inside the rear door — shoe size 10.5. Webb wears size 9. (6) No security cameras exist anywhere in the alley. ANALYST CONCLUSION: \u0027The rear door was an easily accessible, unsecured entry point. It is entirely consistent with a third-party entry and exit. The physical evidence at the rear door — different shoe size, different cigarette brands — suggests someone other than Marcus Webb used that entrance.\u0027",
